  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Xcolor command (code $0a). Shows the label XCOLOR. On a button press, reads the colour of the pixel under the cursor into target_colour and replaces it with current_colour in all of the picture. When target_colour is the background colour, the background colour ($d021, background_colour) becomes current_colour, and clear_colour_pixels runs for the old and for the new colour. Else each screen nybble and colour RAM value that is target_colour becomes current_colour. When current_colour is the background colour, clear_colour_pixels runs in place of the replacement. A long press off the pad goes to tool_exit."},
    {"at":53,"placement":"side","text":"Pixel value to colour."},
    {"at":161,"placement":"line","text":"Increments cell_screen_ptr and cell_colour_ptr. Z = 1 when cell_colour_ptr is $dbe8, after the last of the 1000 cells."},
    {"at":184,"placement":"line","text":"Sets cell_screen_ptr to $5c00 and cell_colour_ptr to $d800, the first cell."},
    {"at":201,"placement":"line","text":"For each of the 1000 cells: each pixel value (1-3) whose cell colour is target_colour gets its pixels set to 0, the background (clear_slot_pixels)."},
    {"at":246,"placement":"line","text":"A = pixel value (1-3). In the 8 bitmap bytes of the cell of cell_screen_ptr ($6000 + 8 * cell number), sets each pixel with this value to 0."},
    {"at":248,"placement":"side","text":"work_ptr = (cell_screen_ptr AND $03ff) * 8 + $6000."},
    {"at":303,"placement":"side","text":"ASL and ADC #0 two times: rotates the byte left by 2 bits."}
  ],
